+Two postmenopausal patients with labial and clitoral-hood agglutination had oxidized regenerated cellulose sutured over the separated surfaces; neither had reagglutination after more than 18 months.<sup>[[26]](#ref26)</sup> This barrier approach has been reported for dense recurrent fusion after **sharp** separation, whereas thin prepuce-to-glans adhesions are generally separated **bluntly** in the office.<sup>[[11]](#ref11)[[26]](#ref26)[[4]](#ref4)</sup>
